  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 208 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nA dry cold front is expected to pass on Sunday. Its passage will \nonly serve to briefly stunt the warming trend on Monday, keeping \nhighs in the upper 60s to mid-70s as opposed to the 80s we'd likely \nsee without its influence. Temperatures will rebound quickly, though \ndue to the increasing influence of mid-level ridging and daily \ninsolation. Confidence is high that we'll see widespread highs in \nthe 80s again by Wednesday. LREF probabilities of >79 degrees at 1pm \nWednesday are 50-70% south of I-70, and this isn't even capturing \npeak heating. The same NBM probabilities at 4pm call for a 50-90% \nchance south of US 36/I-72, and its IQR spread through Wednesday is \nonly 3-5 degrees. This new regime will keep the forecast dry through \nthe period as well. Ensemble guidance between now and late next week \nshow peak PoPs of 20%, and those are from the most excited models. \nOverall, expect dry and warming conditions until further notice.",
